<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">01 · Hoshizaki commercial refrigerator not cooling</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Hot-gas defrost specialists. Three root causes we diagnose first.</h2>

    <p>A Hoshizaki commercial refrigerator that won't hold below 41°F usually traces to one of three root causes our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair diagnose first across LA County Japanese restaurants, sushi bars, ramen shops, premium hospitality, and pharmacy/lab cold storage installations. (1) Condenser fan motor failure year 8 to 12 — even on Hoshizaki Japanese engineering build quality, the most common single service item across CR-Series, HR-Series, CRMR prep tables, and HUR undercounter. $320 to $580 replacement. (2) Dirty condenser coil — kitchen grease and lint accumulate on the condenser fins. About 20 to 25 percent of Hoshizaki calls resolve at the $120 commercial diagnostic with cleaning, no parts charge. (3) Inverter compressor diagnostic on HR-Series and HF-Series premium tier — inverter-driven compressors require specific diagnostic protocol vs standard CR/CF non-inverter units. Different amp draw patterns under variable-speed operation.</p>

    <p><strong>This page covers Hoshizaki commercial refrigeration (CR / CF reach-in, HR / HF premium reach-in, CRMR prep tables, HUR / HUF undercounter, HPR pharmacy UL listed) — separate from Hoshizaki ice machine line, which we service via the <a href="/commercial/ice-machines/">commercial ice machine service hub</a>.</strong> Same parent company (Hoshizaki Corporation Japan, founded 1947 Toyoake; US HQ Peachtree City Georgia), separate equipment categories, separate parts catalogs, separate service procedures.</p>

    <p>Critical Hoshizaki brand-specific knowledge: <strong>Hoshizaki freezers don't have defrost heaters.</strong> They use hot-gas defrost — refrigerant flow reverses during the defrost cycle to melt frost off the evaporator coil. Most repair shops misdiagnose Hoshizaki freezer defrost failures as "needs new heater" because they don't know the brand. The actual issue on Hoshizaki freezer defrost faults is the defrost solenoid valve (controls hot-gas flow direction), defrost timer (controls cycle initiation), or reversing valve (controls refrigerant flow direction). Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair diagnose Hoshizaki hot-gas defrost correctly. See the broader <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/brands/hoshizaki/">Hoshizaki brand pillar</a> for full lineup context.</p>

    <p><strong>$120 commercial diagnostic, applied toward repair.</strong> BHGS Registration #A49573 and EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410), plus R-290 propane certification for Hoshizaki post-2018 green-refrigerant models. CSLB C-20 HVAC. BBB Accredited Business. 90-day warranty. Same-day across LA, OC, Ventura. Next-day Riverside and San Bernardino. Sister sub-services: <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/walk-in-cooler-not-cooling/">walk-in cooler not cooling</a>, <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/true-refrigerator-not-cooling/">True refrigerator not cooling</a>, <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/traulsen-refrigerator-not-cooling/">Traulsen refrigerator not cooling</a>. Parent: <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/">commercial refrigeration</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 02 DIAGNOSTIC SEQUENCE -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">02 · Five-step diagnostic on every Hoshizaki not-cooling call</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Brand-specific sequence — hot-gas defrost first on freezer variants.</h2>

    <ol class="num-list">
      <li><strong>Box temperature documentation.</strong> Probe at product level to verify current product temperature against operator log. CalCode 41°F threshold for refrigerator variants; USDA 0°F federal floor for freezer variants. Pharmacy HPR units additionally require continuous temperature monitoring alarm contact verification.</li>
      <li><strong>Identify series and refrigerant.</strong> CR / CF standard tier, HR / HF premium with inverter, CRMR prep, HUR / HUF undercounter, HPR pharmacy. Refrigerant (R-134a refrigerator or R-404A freezer legacy, R-290 propane post-2018) determines certification requirement.</li>
      <li><strong>Visual condenser inspection.</strong> Kitchen grease, dust, lint accumulation on fins. If condenser is the diagnosis, cleaning runs $200 to $280 and resolves the call without parts on 20 to 25 percent of LA Hoshizaki service visits.</li>
      <li><strong>Condenser fan motor amp draw and rotation.</strong> Most common single Hoshizaki service item. $320 to $580 replacement. Inverter HR-Series additionally requires inverter compressor diagnostic protocol.</li>
      <li><strong>Hot-gas defrost diagnostic (freezer variants only).</strong> Defrost solenoid valve continuity, defrost timer initiation cycle, reversing valve operation under defrost call. NOT defrost heater (which doesn't exist on Hoshizaki freezers). Most-misdiagnosed Hoshizaki failure mode by other shops.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>Most diagnostics complete in 25 to 40 minutes on-site. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair walk operators through the findings with photo documentation before any repair work begins. Sealed-system work on R-290 propane Hoshizaki models requires both EPA 608 Universal certification (#1346255700410) and R-290 hydrocarbon certification.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 03 TOP CAUSES FREQUENCY -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">03 · Top causes by frequency</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Across LA County Hoshizaki commercial refrigeration calls.</h2>

    <p>Across LA County Hoshizaki commercial refrigeration service calls our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair run — Sawtelle Japantown sushi bars with full Hoshizaki kitchens, Little Tokyo DTLA ramen shops and Japanese restaurants, West LA sushi-row corridor premium hospitality, Beverly Hills luxury hospitality, Newport Beach premium Japanese restaurants, plus hospital pharmacy and lab HPR-Series institutional installations across Pasadena and Los Angeles medical centers — the failure breakdown clusters predictably.</p>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>1. Condenser fan motor failure (25-30% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Most common single Hoshizaki service item across all series. Year 8 to 12 typical wear curve. Head pressure climbs without fan circulation, cooling capacity drops. $320 to $580 replacement, same-day from truck stock.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>2. Dirty condenser coil (20-25% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Restaurant kitchen grease, dust, lint accumulate on condenser fins. Resolves at the $120 commercial diagnostic with cleaning on 20 to 25 percent of Hoshizaki service calls, no parts charge. Standalone deep cleaning $200 to $280.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>3. Hot-gas defrost component failure — freezer variants (15-20% of freezer calls)</h3>
      <p>Defrost solenoid valve, defrost timer, or reversing valve. The most-misdiagnosed Hoshizaki failure mode by other shops who quote "defrost heater replacement" not knowing Hoshizaki freezers don't have heaters. $280 to $640 typical depending on component. Our techs diagnose correctly.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>4. Inverter compressor diagnostic — HR/HF premium tier (10-15% of HR calls)</h3>
      <p>HR-Series and HF-Series premium tier use inverter-driven compressors for variable-speed operation. Different diagnostic protocol than standard CR/CF non-inverter. Variable amp draw patterns under different load conditions. Specific inverter board fault codes when applicable. Diagnostic complexity higher than standard reach-in compressor work.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>5. Door gasket year 6-8 (10-12% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Compression set, tearing, magnetic seal failure. Hoshizaki Japanese-spec gaskets last longer than mid-tier (year 6-8 vs year 4-6 mid-tier). $180 to $340 replacement covering CR, HR, CRMR, HUR dimensions stocked on truck.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>6. Compressor failure CR year 10-13 / HR year 12-18 (8-10% of calls)</h3>
      <p>CR-Series compressor $1,400 to $2,200 all-in. HR-Series inverter compressor $1,800 to $2,800. CRMR prep $1,400 to $2,000. HUR undercounter $1,000 to $1,600. HPR pharmacy UL-listed $2,000 to $2,800. Higher pricing on HR-Series reflects inverter compressor parts pipeline plus Japan-assembled premium component sourcing.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

